---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Diagram from "../../components/Diagram.astro";
import Excerpt from "../../components/Excerpt.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import Routes from "../../components/Routes.astro";
import { page } from "../../lib/nav.ts";

const M = "server/src/iki_server/runs/models.py";
const SV = "server/src/iki_server/runs/services.py";
const Q = "server/src/iki_server/runs/queue.py";
const R = "server/src/iki_server/runs/results.py";
const J = "worker/crates/iki-worker/src/job.rs";

const launching = page("Launching a run").href;
const worker = page("The worker and its leases").href;
const tiers = page("Compute tiers").href;
const pinning = page("Pinning and provenance").href;

const boxes = [
  { id: "manifest", x: 20, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Action manifest", sub: "a plugin's actions/*.yaml", href: page("What a plugin declares").href },
  { id: "launch", x: 200, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Launch", sub: "everything checked first", strong: true, href: launching },
  { id: "queued", x: 380, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Run and Job", sub: "queued in Postgres", href: launching },
  { id: "lease", x: 560, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Lease", sub: "a fenced token", href: worker },
  { id: "worker", x: 740, y: 40, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Worker", sub: "runs the command", href: worker },
  { id: "reuse", x: 200, y: 180, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Reuse", sub: "same key, earlier results", href: pinning },
  { id: "approval", x: 380, y: 180, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Approval", sub: "an agent's costly run", href: launching },
  { id: "provisioner", x: 560, y: 180, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Provisioner", sub: "starts pods, VMs", href: tiers },
  { id: "outputs", x: 740, y: 180, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Outputs", sub: "uploaded; complete", href: worker },
  { id: "records", x: 380, y: 310, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Records", sub: "revisions, effects, lineage", href: pinning },
  { id: "results", x: 560, y: 310, w: 150, h: 60, label: "Results", sub: "checked, all or nothing", strong: true, href: pinning },
];
const edges = [
  { from: "manifest", to: "launch" },
  { from: "launch", to: "queued" },
  { from: "queued", to: "lease" },
  { from: "lease", to: "worker" },
  { from: "launch", to: "reuse", label: "deterministic", dashed: true },
  { from: "launch", to: "approval", label: "if unattended", dashed: true },
  { from: "approval", to: "queued", label: "approved" },
  { from: "queued", to: "provisioner", label: "container, vm", dashed: true },
  { from: "provisioner", to: "worker", label: "starts one" },
  { from: "worker", to: "outputs" },
  { from: "outputs", to: "results", label: "POST complete" },
  { from: "results", to: "records" },
  { from: "reuse", to: "records", label: "reused effects", dashed: true },
  { from: "worker", to: "queued", label: "retry: a new Job", dashed: true, via: [[815, 16], [455, 16]] as [number, number][] },
];

const H = {
  short: "What a run is",
  how: "How the parts fit",
  example: "Finding an antibody chain's liabilities",
  ref: "Routes, code and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "example", label: H.example },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      A run is one request to run a plugin's action on some records. Everything that could make it
      fail for a reason other than its own work is checked before it's queued. It's then one <code
        >ActionRun</code
      >, however many attempts it takes; each attempt is a <code>Job</code> that a worker leases over
      HTTPS with a token only it holds. The worker runs exactly the plugin code the run was launched
      with, on the records it pinned. Its outputs are checked against what the action declared, then
      written all at once, as revisions that name the run. A deterministic run with the same inputs
      as an earlier one reuses that one's results instead of running.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>A run records what was asked; jobs are its attempts (<Adr n="0042" />).</li>
      <li>Workers pull, under fenced leases (<Adr n="0043" />).</li>
      <li>Results are checked, then written all or nothing (<Adr n="0044" />).</li>
      <li>Identical deterministic runs reuse results; any run can be reproduced exactly (<Adr n="0057" />).</li>
    </ul>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <p>
      The launch writes the run and its first job in one transaction and wakes that tier's workers
      with <code>pg_notify</code>. Container- and vm-tier jobs also wake the provisioner, which starts
      a machine whose worker then leases the job. The worker reports through heartbeats, uploads its
      files straight to object storage, and posts its output. The server checks the output and
      writes it, or ends the attempt; a retryable ending queues a new job. Click a box for its files;
      "Its section" goes to the page that covers it.
    </p>
    <Diagram id="runlife" title="A run's life" width={910} height={390} boxes={boxes} edges={edges}>
      <div slot="manifest">
        <p>
          Inputs, params, effects, where it runs (<code>runs_on</code>), its command, network hosts,
          secrets, and whether it's deterministic, batchable or checkpointable (<Adr n="0040" />).
        </p>
        <p><Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/actions.py" sym="def read_action(" />, <Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/model.py" sym="class Action:" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="launch">
        <p>The tier permission, inputs, params, references and project, outside APIs, reuse, budgets, approval and quota, in that order (<Adr n={[42, 66]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p={SV} sym="def launch(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="queued">
        <p>The run pins the plugin's commit, the action as installed and each input at its revision; one <code>Job</code> is queued.</p>
        <p><Path p={M} sym="class ActionRun(" />, <Path p={M} sym="class Job(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="lease">
        <p>A worker takes the best job it can run, with a new token and a 60-second expiry (<Adr n={[43, 108]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p={Q} sym="def lease(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="worker">
        <p>Stages the input, runs the command in its own process group, and stops it on cancel, timeout or a lost lease (<Adr n="0046" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={J} sym="pub fn run(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="reuse">
        <p>A deterministic run whose reuse key matches an earlier success ends at once with its results (<Adr n="0057" />).</p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/runs/reuse.py" sym="def find(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="approval">
        <p>A run from MCP or a trigger on a costly tier, or sending data to outside APIs, waits for its person (<Adr n={[13, 50]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/runs/approvals.py" sym="def needed(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="provisioner">
        <p>Starts a pod or a cloud machine for queued work no free machine can take (<Adr n={[61, 74]} />).</p>
        <p><Path p="server/src/iki_server/runs/provisioner.py" sym="def tick(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="outputs">
        <p>Files go to object storage by signed URLs; then <code>output.json</code> goes to <code>complete</code>, or a reason to <code>fail</code>.</p>
        <p><Path p={Q} sym="def complete(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="results">
        <p>Checked against the run's own copy of the action, then written in one transaction as the launcher (<Adr n="0044" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={R} sym="def checked(" />, <Path p={R} sym="def write(" /></p>
      </div>
      <div slot="records">
        <p>Each record touched gets a <code>RunEffect</code>; each new one gets <code>Lineage</code> to its inputs (<Adr n="0035" />).</p>
        <p><Path p={M} sym="class RunEffect(" />, <Path p={M} sym="class Lineage(" /></p>
      </div>
    </Diagram>
    <p>
      Three pages cover what surrounds that path: <PageLink to="Network and secrets" /> (what a
      command may reach and the secrets it gets), <PageLink to="Quotas and cost" /> (what limits
      runs and what they cost) and <PageLink to="Workflows and triggers" /> (runs launched by other
      runs, by changes, or on a schedule).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={3} title={H.example}>
    <p>
      A scientist asks Iki to find the sequence liabilities of an antibody chain. The action is <Path
        p="plugins/antibody/actions/find_liabilities.yaml"
        label="iki/antibody.find_liabilities"
      />:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file="plugins/antibody/actions/find_liabilities.yaml" start="^inputs:" rest note="from inputs: on" />
    <ol>
      <li>
        The browser posts to <code>POST /api/v1/actions/{"{name}"}/runs</code>. The server checks the
        tier permission, the input and that it's in the run's project, then writes an{" "}
        <code>ActionRun</code> and one <code>Job</code> and sends <code>pg_notify</code> on{" "}
        <code>iki_jobs</code> (<PageLink to="Launching a run" />).
      </li>
      <li>
        A backend worker's long poll on <code>/worker/v1/lease</code> wakes, and the server hands it
        the job with a fresh lease token. Had the chain been one of a batch, up to 499 more of its
        queued jobs would have been packed into this one, since the action is <code
          >batchable: 500</code
        > (<PageLink to="The worker and its leases" />).
      </li>
      <li>
        The worker runs <code>python ./scripts/liabilities.py</code> with the run's input file,
        heartbeating every 20 seconds, and stops it at the ten-minute <code>timeout</code>. It posts
        the output to <code>/worker/v1/jobs/{"{job_id}"}/complete</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        The server checks that the output updates only the three fields <code>effects.updates</code>{" "}
        names on that input, then writes the protein's new revision in one transaction, recording the
        run as its provenance. Anything else in the output fails the run as <code>invalid_output</code>;
        if the plugin's type changed meanwhile so the results no longer fit
        (<code>schema: "&gt;=2"</code>), the run is <code>rejected</code> instead (<PageLink
          to="Pinning and provenance"
        />).
      </li>
      <li>
        The browser hears the change and refetches (<PageLink to="Tasks and live updates" />).
        Because the action is <code>deterministic: true</code>, the same request on the same revision
        later reuses this run's result instead of running again.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      It declares no <code>network</code>, so its command reaches no host, and no{" "}
      <code>retries</code>, so a run whose worker was lost or interrupted is retried up to twice
      (<Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/actions.py" sym="retry_max=" />). The environment it names runs on
      the backend and self-hosted tiers:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file="plugins/antibody/environments/antibody-tools.yaml" start="^tiers:" rest note="from tiers: on" />
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <h3>Public routes for runs</h3>
    <Routes tags={["runs"]} />
    <div class="refs">
      <div>
        <h3>Where</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/runs" /></li>
          <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/runs.py" /></li>
          <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/worker.py" /></li>
          <li><Path p="worker/crates/iki-worker/src" /></li>
          <li><Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/actions.py" /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Decisions</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><Adr n="0040" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0042" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0043" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0044" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0057" title /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
